/* LEVEL-4-START */
["Console","The restaurant’s back office","Anthropic’s website for builders, at platform.claude.com: API keys, usage, limits, billing and a place to try requests.","Not the Claude app at claude.ai. That’s the dining room.",1,"Make a key in the Console and set a spend limit.",4],
["Playground","The test kitchen","The Console page where you try a request, see its usage and copy the same request as code. It replaced the old Workbench.","Not saved history. Your draft stays in your browser.",1,"Try it in the playground first, then grab the code.",4],
["Environment variable","The key on a hook behind the counter","A named setting your computer or server holds outside your code. The SDK reads your key from ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.","Not a line in your code. That’s how keys leak.",1,"Did you set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY?",4],
["Model ID","The chef’s exact name on the slip","The exact text that picks a model in a request, like claude-opus-5-5.","Not the friendly name. “Opus” alone won’t work.",1,"Swap the model ID to claude-haiku-5-5 and rerun.",4],
["Content block","One item on the plate","The reply’s content is a list of blocks: text, thinking, tool use and more. Check each block’s type before reading it.","Not one plain string of text.",1,"Loop over the content blocks and print the text ones.",4],
["Usage","The receipt","The part of every reply that counts input and output tokens, plus cache reads and writes. You price calls from it.","Not your monthly bill. It’s one call.",1,"Log usage on every call so we can see cost per user.",4],
["MTok","Prices by the million","A million tokens. API prices are per MTok: Opus 5.5 costs $4 per MTok in and $20 out.","Not a thousand. 1,000 tokens is a thousandth of an MTok.",2,"Haiku is ten cents per MTok in.",4],
["Adaptive thinking","The chef decides how long to think","Claude decides how much to think on each request. Effort sets how far it may go. On Opus 5.5 it’s always on.","Not a setting that makes it learn from you.",2,"Adaptive thinking is on; just lower the effort.",4],
["Time to first token","How soon the first bite arrives","How long from sending a request until the first piece of the reply appears. Streaming makes it visible.","Not the total time for the whole reply.",2,"Time to first token is fine; it’s the long answers that drag.",4],
["Model routing","The host who seats each guest","Sorting each request first, then sending easy ones to a small, cheap model and hard ones to a bigger one.","Not running every request on every model.",2,"Route the simple questions to Haiku.",4],
["Fast mode","A faster line at a higher price","An option on some models, Opus 5.5 among them, for up to 2.5x faster output at a premium price.","Not a smaller model. Same chef, faster hands.",2,"Turn on fast mode for the live demo only.",4],
["JSON Schema","The plate diagram","A standard way to describe data: which fields, which types, which are required.","Not the data itself. It’s the shape the data must fit.",3,"Send me the JSON Schema for the receipt fields.",4],
["output_config","The plating instructions on the slip","The request field that holds settings for the reply, like format (a JSON schema) and effort.","Not the system prompt. It sets rules the API enforces.",3,"Put the schema in output_config.format.",4],
["Strict tool use","Appliance inputs that always fit","Setting strict: true on a tool so the inputs Claude sends always match its schema.","Not forcing Claude to call the tool.",3,"Mark the booking tool strict so dates always parse.",4],
["Validation","Checking the plate before it leaves","Code that checks a reply is complete and correct in shape before your app uses it.","Not checking the facts. Right shape can hold a wrong number.",3,"Validate the output before writing it to the database.",4],
["Refusal","The chef sends the order back","A stop_reason meaning Claude declined for safety reasons. The reply may not match your schema.","Not an error code. The call succeeded.",3,"Handle stop_reason refusal before you parse.",4],
["tool_use block","Claude’s order for an appliance","The part of a reply where Claude asks your code to run a tool, with the tool’s name, inputs and an id.","Not the tool running. Your code still has to run it.",4,"Loop over the tool_use blocks and run each one.",4],
["tool_result block","The appliance’s answer, sent back","What your code sends back after running a tool, tagged with the matching tool_use_id.","Not Claude’s final answer.",4,"You forgot the tool_result for the second call.",4],
["tool_choice","Whether the chef may use appliances","The request setting for tools: auto (Claude decides, the default) or none. Forcing a tool errors on Opus 5.5.","Not the list of tools. That’s the tools array.",4,"Leave tool_choice on auto and name the tool in the prompt.",4],
["Parallel tool calls","Two appliance orders at once","Claude asking for several tools in one reply. Send all the results back in one message.","Not a loop of single calls.",4,"It made parallel tool calls, so batch the results.",4],
["Server tool","An appliance Anthropic runs","A tool that runs on Anthropic’s servers, like web search or code execution. You add it; you don’t code it.","Not your own tool. Your code doesn’t run it.",4,"Web search is a server tool, so no handler needed.",4],
["Tool Runner","A helper that runs the loop for you","An SDK feature (beta) that calls Claude, runs your tool functions and sends results back until Claude is done.","Not a different API. It’s a helper inside the SDK.",4,"Use the Tool Runner instead of a hand-written loop.",4],
["cache_control","The “prepped, reuse it” sticker","The marker that tells the API to cache your prompt up to that point, so repeat calls read it cheaply.","Not saving the answer. It saves the prompt’s start.",5,"Put cache_control on the last system block.",4],
["Cache TTL","How long prep stays fresh","Time to live: how long a cache entry lasts. 5 minutes by default; 1 hour costs more to write.","Not forever. Unused prep expires.",5,"Use the 1-hour TTL; users come back after 20 minutes.",4],
["Cache hit","Prep pulled from the fridge","A request that reads its start from the cache. It shows as cache_read_input_tokens above zero.","Not the same as a cache write, which costs more.",5,"Our cache hit rate dropped after the last deploy.",4],
["Token counting","Weighing the order before cooking","A free API endpoint (count_tokens) that estimates how many input tokens a request will use, for a given model.","Not a word count. Tokens aren’t words.",5,"Count tokens before you send the whole manual.",4],
["custom_id","The table number on each batch order","The tag you give each request in a Message Batch, so you can match every result to its request. Results can come back in any order.","Not the batch’s own id.",5,"Use the review’s database id as the custom_id.",4],
["Files API","The storeroom","Upload a file once and get a file_id you can reuse in later requests, instead of sending the file every time.","Not a search index. Claude still reads what you point it to.",6,"Upload the PDF with the Files API and reuse the file_id.",4],
["Document block","A book handed to the chef","A content block that gives Claude a PDF or text document, optionally with citations turned on.","Not a plain text message.",6,"Send it as a document block with citations enabled.",4],
["Voyage AI","The catalogue maker next door","The embeddings company Anthropic’s docs point to, now part of MongoDB. Anthropic has no embedding model of its own.","Not a Claude model.",6,"We embed the chunks with Voyage.",4],
["BM25","Searching the index by exact word","A classic keyword search that ranks text by matching words. Often paired with embeddings in RAG.","Not meaning-based. It misses synonyms.",6,"Add BM25 so exact product codes still match.",4],
["Reranker","The sous-chef who picks the best five","A model that takes a question and candidate chunks and sorts them by how well they answer it.","Not the search itself. It sorts what search found.",6,"Retrieve 150, rerank, keep the top 20.",4],
["Contextual retrieval","A label on every recipe card","Adding a short note to each chunk, before indexing, that says where it fits in its document.","Not a bigger context window.",6,"Contextual retrieval fixed the orphan chunks.",4],
["Code grader","A thermometer, not a taster","A test check written in code, like an exact match or a schema check. Free, fast, consistent.","Not an AI judge. It can’t judge tone.",7,"Use a code grader for the labels.",4],
["Rubric","The judge’s scoring sheet","The written criteria a judge scores one answer against.","Not the test cases. It’s how they’re scored.",7,"Tighten the rubric; the judge is too generous.",4],
["Pairwise comparison","Two plates, pick the better","A judge reads two answers to the same input and picks the better one.","Not scoring each answer alone.",7,"Run a pairwise comparison against the old prompt.",4],
["Baseline","Last night’s scores, kept","The results of the current version, saved so every change can be compared against them.","Not the best possible score.",7,"What did the baseline get on case 12?",4],
["Pass rate","Plates that passed out of all plates","The share of test cases that passed, like 46 of 50.","Not the whole story. Check cost and time too.",7,"The pass rate went up but so did the cost.",4],
["Overloaded error","The kitchen is slammed","HTTP 529, overloaded_error: Anthropic is busy. Not your mistake. Retry with backoff.","Not a 429, which is about your own limits.",8,"We got 529s during the spike, so the retries kicked in.",4],
["Exponential backoff","Wait longer before each retry","Retrying after waits that grow, like 1, 2, 4 seconds, often with a random extra (jitter).","Not retrying instantly in a tight loop.",8,"Add exponential backoff with jitter.",4],
["retry-after","The sign: back in 30 seconds","A response header that says how many seconds to wait before trying again.","Not always there. A spend-cap 429 never has it.",8,"Respect retry-after instead of guessing.",4],
["Spend limit","A cap on the monthly bill","A monthly ceiling on API spend. Each tier has one, and you can set your own lower limit in the Console.","Not a rate limit, which is per minute.",8,"Set a spend limit before launch.",4],
["Request ID","The ticket number","The id on every API response, like req_018…. Log it so support can find the exact call.","Not your API key. Safe to share with support.",8,"Send support the request ID from the failed call.",4]
